menu "Watch OS"

    config WATCH_REMOTE_UI
        bool "Remote screen through the authenticated web API"
        default y
        select LV_USE_SNAPSHOT

    config WATCH_MONKEY_TEST
        bool "Monkey test (random swipes, apps, screen on/off)"
        default n
        help
            Stress test for development: after the boot a task plays with
            the UI forever (no taps, only safe apps) and logs a health report
            every minute. Never enable it in a release.

    config WATCH_DEV_CONSOLE
        bool "Development console (screenshots, open apps, readings over USB)"
        default n
        select LV_USE_SNAPSHOT
        help
            Commands typed on the console drive the UI and print readings, for
            testing from the PC (tools/devcon.py in the firmware repos). Anyone
            with a USB cable could use it: never enable it in a release.

    config WATCH_LV_BAND_LINES
        int "LVGL bands drawn in PSRAM (lines, 0 = off)"
        default 0
        range 0 480
        help
            LVGL walks every widget once per band it draws, so many short bands
            (BOARD_DRAW_BUFFER_LINES) make swipes slow. With a value here LVGL draws
            two bands this tall in PSRAM and a sender task copies them through the
            internal DMA buffers to the panel: same internal RAM, far fewer passes.
            Only for panels fed by DMA (SPI/QSPI); with a rotated screen the
            sender also rotates each piece.
            Pick about a quarter of the panel height, rounded to an even number.

endmenu
